cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: "BOLT: Browser-Only Labelling Tool"
abstract: >-
  BOLT (Browser-Only Labelling Tool) is a single-file web application for
  expert review of provisional text annotations, such as variables extracted
  from clinical notes by a large language model. Users define a schema of
  variables and permissible labels, then load source documents and
  annotations from CSV files with configurable column mapping. For each
  document, BOLT displays the text alongside one card per annotation,
  highlights the supporting evidence in the text and flags evidence that
  cannot be located. Reviewers mark each annotation as correct, correct it
  with a new classification or evidence span, reject it outright, or add
  annotations the model missed. Decisions are exported to CSV with the
  original and corrected values side by side, and a saved export can be
  reloaded to resume a review. BOLT runs entirely in the browser from a local
  HTML file, with no installation, server or network connection, so
  sensitive text never leaves the reviewer's computer.
